{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "use_case": "openzeppelin-safecast",
  "source": "openzeppelin-contracts utils/math/SafeCast.sol, against a harness that exposes each cast",
  "note": "Each cast reverts exactly when the value does not fit, so each is written as two rules, one per direction. The property language compares words, not signed values, so a signed bound is written as the words it admits: `value < 0` over an `int256` is `value >= 2^255`, and `-128 <= value <= 127` is `value <= 127 or value >= 2^256-128`. That is the same statement, and it is the one the EVM makes. Every rule is expected to hold.",
  "call_properties": [
